Cache: Context

Purpose:
  Defines context caching policy, invalidation, and optimization
  metrics.

CacheStructure:
  context-id:
    source: <list of sources>
    hash: <content hash>
    last-used: <timestamp>
    dependencies: <list of dependent contexts>

CacheRules:
  [CC1]  Context MUST be cached to avoid re-analysis.
  [CC2]  Cache hit occurs when source unchanged (hash matches).
  [CC3]  Cache miss triggers re-build from scratch.
  [CC4]  Cache invalidation follows dependency graph.

CacheHit:
  Source unchanged
    ↓
  CACHE HIT
    ↓
  Reuse cached context

CacheMiss:
  Source changed
    ↓
  CACHE MISS
    ↓
  Rebuild context

OptimizationMetrics:
  ContextTokens:
    Total tokens loaded
  RelevantTokens:
    Tokens actually used
  UnusedTokens:
    Tokens loaded but not used
  ContextHitRate:
    Cache hits / total requests
  ContextMissRate:
    Cache misses / total requests
  ExpansionCount:
    Number of progressive expansions
  CacheHitRate:
    Cached contexts reused / total contexts

ContextEfficiency:
  Formula:
    Relevant Context / Total Context

  Target:
    > 80%

  Note:
    Safety-critical tasks MUST NOT sacrifice relevance for efficiency.

State: +
  